<Page title="Cookie Policy | RDB Building Services LTD" description="Cookies and similar technologies on the current RDB website. No application analytics, advertising cookies or persistent browser storage are configured.">
<section class="wrap service-intro"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Cookies</span></div><p class="eyebrow">COOKIES &amp; SIMILAR TECHNOLOGIES</p><h1>Cookie Policy</h1></section>
<article class="wrap legal-content"><div class="policy-status"><strong>No optional tracking is configured</strong><p>The current production application does not set cookies or use local storage, session storage, advertising pixels or analytics. Submitting an enquiry takes you to FormSubmit, which may use its own cookies and spam-check technologies. These are not embedded in the RDB pages.</p></div>
<h2>What are cookies?</h2><p>Cookies are small pieces of information a website can store in your browser. Similar technologies can store or access device information in other ways. Their purposes can include remembering preferences, providing essential functionality or measuring activity.</p>
<h2>What the current website uses</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Cookie information table; scroll horizontally on small screens"><table class="cookie-table"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Current behaviour</th><th>Application storage duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Analytics and advertising</td><td>Not installed or requested by this application</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Preference and session cookies</td><td>No cookies set by application code</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Local and session storage</td><td>Not used by application code</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Enquiry processing</td><td>Submitted to FormSubmit when you select Send enquiry; its hosted processing and spam-check step may use cookies</td><td>No application browser storage; external service practices apply after submission</td></tr><tr><td>Maps and external guidance</td><td>Ordinary external links; no embedded map or tracking content</td><td>None set by this application</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Why there is no consent pop-up</h2><p>This version does not use optional cookies or tracking technologies, so it does not ask for consent to features it does not have. You can browse our pages without making a cookie choice. When you submit an enquiry, you visit FormSubmit’s external processing step. Its cookies and any spam-check technologies are subject to the information and controls provided there. Browser caching and autofill are managed by your browser or device.</p>
<h2>FormSubmit and external websites</h2><p>Forms submit to FormSubmit only when you choose to send an enquiry. Read <a href="https://formsubmit.co/privacy.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FormSubmit’s privacy information</a> for its cookie and processing practices.</p><p>When you follow a map or guidance link, the destination website may use its own cookies or technologies. Its own notice and controls apply. Those services are not loaded simply by viewing this website.</p>
<h2>Changes to website features</h2><p>If features requiring cookie consent are introduced, they must remain inactive until a valid choice is made. Visitors must be able to reject optional use and change their choice easily. The policy and controls must be updated together.</p><h2>Your browser controls</h2><p>Your browser settings let you inspect and delete cookies and site data. The steps depend on the browser you use. Because this version stores no application cookie preferences, there is no saved consent record or preference to reset here.</p>
<h2>Questions</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk">info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk</a> with cookie questions. Read the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for information about enquiry processing and your rights. You can also read the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/direct-marketing-and-privacy-and-electronic-communications/guide-to-pecr/cookies-and-similar-technologies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ICO’s guidance on cookies and similar technologies</a>.</p>
</article></Page>
